.TH GIT-TCR 1 "2026-09-08" "git-tcr 0.8.0" "git-tcr Manual"
.SH NAME
git-tcr \- Test && Commit || Revert, as a git subcommand
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git tcr
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B git tcr init
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B TCR
(Test && Commit || Revert) is a variation of test-driven development that
forces taking small, incremental steps: if tests pass, the changes are
committed; if they fail, the changes are reverted.
.PP
Running
.B git tcr
with no arguments stages the working tree, runs the test command(s)
configured in
.IR tcr.yaml ,
and either commits the change or discards it, depending on the result.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-message " " \fIMESSAGE\fR
Use a custom commit message instead of the default
.BR WIP .
.TP
.BR \-\-trailer " " \fITRAILER\fR
Append a git trailer to the commit message (e.g.
.IR "Issue: GDT-42" ).
Can be repeated multiple times.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the git-tcr version. The long form
.RB ( \-\-version )
also names the highest
.I tcr.yaml
schema version this build understands.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Interactively create a
.I tcr.yaml
configuration file: prompts for one or more test commands and whether
commits should skip git hooks with
.BR \-\-no\-verify ,
then writes the file. Asks before overwriting an existing one.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B git tcr
reads its configuration from
.I tcr.yaml
in the root of the working tree. Run
.B git tcr init
to create it interactively, or write it by hand:
.PP
.RS
.nf
version: 1
test:
    program: "cargo"
    args: ["test"]
no_verify: false
.fi
.RE
.PP
To run multiple test commands, declare
.B test
as a list instead; commands run in order and stop at the first failure:
.PP
.RS
.nf
test:
    \- program: "tsc"
      args: ["\-\-noEmit"]
    \- program: "npm"
      args: ["run", "test"]
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Run TCR with the default WIP commit message:
.PP
.RS
.nf
git tcr
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run TCR with a custom commit message:
.PP
.RS
.nf
git tcr \-m "feat: add login page"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run TCR with a custom message and one or more trailers:
.PP
.RS
.nf
git tcr \-m "feat: add login page" \-\-trailer "Issue: GDT\-42" \-\-trailer "Reviewed\-by: Alice"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a
.I tcr.yaml
interactively:
.PP
.RS
.nf
git tcr init
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation and source:
.UR https://github.com/sebastianoverdolini/git-tcr
git-tcr on GitHub
.UE .
